title: Young Plan
new-page: true
subtitle: The coalition is nearing collapse...
tags: event
view-if: year = 1929 and month >= 7 and dnvp_in_government
max-visits: 1

= The Young Plan and the fall of the coalition

The Foreign Ministry under [+ foreign_minister +] has agreed to the Young Plan, an agreement with the Western powers to reduce Germany's reparation payments and give us more fiscal autonomy. Simultaneously, France will agree to withdraw its military occupation from the Rhineland.

While this seems to be a positive development for the country, the right wing of the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span>, despite their party's moderation, opposes the plan, claiming that any reparations are a form of national slavery. They have called for a vote of no confidence against the government, supported by the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>, <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span>, and for a referendum on the Young Plan.

The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**[+ spd_name +]**</span> can either vote to bring down the government and hold new elections, or "tolerate" a government led by the remaining bourgeois parties.

- @grand_coalition: Include the <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> in a new cabinet.
- @negotiate: Hold on, perhaps we can reach an agreement to calm them down.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.


@grand_coalition
subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--spd-color);">**SPD**</span> will replace our more right-wing coalition partners.
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; dvp_in_government = 1; dnvp_in_government = 0; spd_toleration = 0; in_center_right_coalition = 0; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = z_name; foreign_minister = "Brüning"; foreign_minister_party = z_name; interior_minister = "Severing"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Guérard"; justice_minister_party = z_name; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser" if ddp_exist; justice_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; labor_minister = "Wissel"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; finance_minister_party = z_name; agriculture_minister = "Hermes"; agriculture_minister_party = z_name; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich" if ddp_exist; agriculture_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; leverage = dvp_r; leverage = 15 if leverage >= 15; dnvp_relation -= 5; spd_relation += 3; dvp_left += 2; liberal_strength += 5; nationalist_dissent += 5;

Heinrich Brüning welcomes us into the new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries.

- @election_1928.ministries: Now, we must select our ministries.

@negotiate
subtitle: We will transfer some resources to the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> and promise to oppose the plan, knowing a referendum has no chance of succeeding. -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: The party will not allow this. [? if dnvp_relation < 40: Our relations with the <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> aren't high enough. ?][? if dnvp_leader == "Hugenberg": Hugenberg isn't interested in negotiating. ?][? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. ?]
choose-if: (liberal_strength*0.5 < (nationalist_strength + industrialist_strength*0.5)) and resources >= 2 and dnvp_relation >= 40 and dnvp_leader != "Hugenberg"
on-arrival: young_plan_dnvp_promise = 1; coalition_dissent += 1; spd_relation -= 5; nationalist_strength += 10; industrialist_strength += 5; liberal_dissent += 20; labor_dissent += 10;

We've managed to persuade the parliamentary <span style="color: var(--dnvp-color);">**[+ dnvp_name +]**</span> to not vote our cabinet down. Besides the resources, we will also need to campaign against the plan. Our liberal wing is outraged, but the coalition holds on for another day.

@new_elections
subtitle: The government will collapse, and there will be new elections.
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; pro_republic -= 2; spd_relation -= 4; z_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; ddp_left += 0.5; dvp_left -= 2; nationalist_strength += 5; liberal_dissent += 5;
call: set_next_election_time

The right-wing coalition has fallen. New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
